<title>USA: YPF sells Canadon Seco at WTI minus $2.47 for Feb.</title>
<headline>YPF sells Canadon Seco at WTI minus $2.47 for Feb.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine oil company YPF sold two cargoes of Canadon Seco crude for late February loading, trade sources said Friday.</p>
<p>Two cargoes of the light crude were dealt at West Texas Intermediate minus $2.47. Each of the cargoes contains 380,000 barrels of Canadon Seco, with the first loading February 23-24, and the second February 27-28.</p>
<p>Both cargoes were headed for Far East destinations, the sources said.</p>
<p>Canadon Seco is a waxy crude with an API gravity of 25.7 degrees and 0.23 percent sulfur. Previous buyers included Brazil's state-owned oil company Petrobras, U.S. Gulf Coast refiners and traders.</p>
<p>--Patrick Connole, New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859 1620</p>
